WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.136
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Roy Wood Jr.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.437
We both work on shows
that talk about the news.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:09.008
I would love to get your take on
the McCarthy vote chaos.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:14.580
-What is -- What's wrong
with our country, man?

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.718
'Cause, like, it's one thing to
laugh about what's happening

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.720
with the Republicans
and not being able to vote on

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.490
the speaker or whatever,
but, also, don't forget,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.193
while this is happening,
government is not happening.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.461
-Yeah.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.530
-Our government has not started.
You're back to work.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.198
-Yeah.
-I'm back to work.

00:00:33.198 --> 00:00:34.868
They're back to work.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.270
Our government
is just still just --

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.372
You ever been at a fast-food
spot during the shift change?

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:42.208
-Uh-huh.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.109
-That's essentially what's
happening in D.C. right now.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:45.544
It's just somebody keep
counting down the register.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:46.846
The money ain't right,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.315
so they got to keep counting
the register again.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.951
And I'm just here
for a little government.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:55.054
I just want a little government
and some fries.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.257
But I just -- I don't --
I really hate that.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.725
I hate the fact that you have
all of these new politicians

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:02.896
who worked hard
during midterms to be elected,

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:05.732
and now they have to sit
and twiddle their thumbs,

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.000
because no one
can even be sworn in.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.201
-Yeah.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.169
-You can't even --
You got the job, and just,

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.371
"Yeah, I'm sorry that..."

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.806
"Hey, you got hired
at 'Seth Meyers,'

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:17.544
but we haven't voted on
a new Seth Meyers yet.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.978
You can't work."

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.180
And so I think
that part of it, I think,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.118
is what is lost in a lot of
the debate on all of this, man.

00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:27.887
But it's fun to watch, though.
-It is fun to watch.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.288
You --

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.724
-Watching Republicans fight like
this, it's like watching --

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.060
You ever seen a family fight
at Golden Corral?

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:36.629
It's like that.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.930
You be like, "I don't want to be
a part of that family,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.468
but that's
an interesting family."

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.970
-It's going to be
an interesting year for

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.171
everyone over at
"The Daily Show."

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.406
Obviously, Trevor announced
he was leaving

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:48.674
after a seven-year run.

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:49.875
In his announcement,

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:52.078
which I believe
caught everybody off guard,

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.579
he mentioned that you
had just --

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.882
-Don't point, don't point,
don't point.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:58.217
-Well, I feel like
I didn't do the pointing,

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:00.420
but Trevor did say
you had just said to him,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.921
"Can you believe
it's been seven years?"

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.956
-That's all --
And that's all I said.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:04.991
That's all I said.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.727
And then the liberal media...

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.762
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:13.199
They somehow took --
Here's what happened.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.700
The day before
Trevor stepped down --

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.936
The day before Trevor announced
that he was going to step down

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:20.439
from the show, I said,
"Hey, man, seven years, man.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:21.640
Today, it's been seven years."

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.377
And he just went...

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:26.679
And I was like,
"What was that [bleep]"

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:27.914
He was like, "Nothing."

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.315
And then, the next day,
he announced.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.251
And I didn't say it
in the sense of,

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:35.788
"Hey, man, you need to get
the hell out of here."

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.190
It's like, imagine if you told
your wife "happy anniversary,"

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.858
and then, the next day,
she was like, "I'm leaving."

00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:42.061
You're like, "What?!"

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:45.964
So, yeah, but, you know,
I'm very happy for him, man.

00:02:45.964 --> 00:02:47.666
I'm happy for him
making that choice for himself.

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:50.236
-I'm happy for him, excited to
see what's next for him.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.871
I know you're going have
a rotation of hosts.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.506
You're going to get to
do it for a week.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.275
I'm looking forward to that.
-At some point.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.376
But, you know,
we got a gang of celebrities

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:58.544
coming in first, man.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.812
-I mean,
there's a lot of big names.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:00.880
Have you worked with
some of these people before?

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.848
-Yeah, it's going to be
a blessing, man,

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:05.117
to really be able to sit down
with the likes of --

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:07.419
I've opened for
these people on the road,

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.689
but to actually sit and create
late-night television

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:14.026
for four days with Wanda Sykes
and Marlon Wayans, Leslie Jones,

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.930
Chelsea Handler,
Sarah Silverman --

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.864
Al Franken is stepping up
in that thing.

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:21.133
The only week
I'm nervous about is Chelsea.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.168
-Uh-huh.
This is Chelsea Handler.

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:24.637
-I'm nervous about
Chelsea Handler week.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.172
-Now, where do
your nerves come from?

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.942
-Because back in '07, I said
some wild [bleep] on her show.

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.209
-Okay.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:32.311
-And you know how you be
a guest on somebody's show,

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:33.513
you say something wild,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.947
and then the producers
don't have you back?

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.148
-Uh-huh.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.349
-And then you be like,
"Man, I ain't gonna never

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:38.584
see her again.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:42.688
It don't matter."
And then I'm like, "Oh [bleep]"

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.857
-Do you remember what you said
that got you in trouble?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.059
-What it was -- Like,
you remember "Chelsea Lately"?

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:50.029
They talked about celebrity,
pop-culture stuff.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:55.034
And I don't remember the year,
but it was a story about

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.635
Sylvester Stallone
getting Botox.

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:57.837
-Uh-huh.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.572
-This was, like, a big --
For the young people,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.541
this was a big conspiracy
back in the day.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.909
Like, "What?

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:06.813
A man with muscles took
something to get more muscles,

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.180
to straighten out his skin?"

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.683
And I don't re--
What I said was to --

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.819
I'm going to just tell you,
because I trust you.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.520
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.722
I said, "Who gives a [bleep]

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:17.890
I like his movies.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.458
I don't care if
he take cocaine."

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:22.662
And whatever it was,
one of the producers --

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.196
Somebody --
Whatever it was, I just --

00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:26.332
I was never invited
back to the show.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.101
And I don't think that was
Chelsea's call,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.935
but it's just
one of those things where

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:32.304
when I'm around Chelsea when she
coming to host "The Daily Show,"

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:35.074
I ain't saying [bleep]
about Sylvester Stallone.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.743
-That's probably very safe.
-My mouth's shut.

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:39.778
But, yeah,
I'm very excited about this.

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:41.247
-When your week
does come around,

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.582
who do you want to interview?

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.083
Who would you
love to sit down with?

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.019
-Oof!

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:48.521
Two people.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.222
Give me Samuel L. Jackson...

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:53.359
-Great choice. A great choice.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.127
-...and Solange Knowles.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:57.730
-Alright. A very...

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:03.068
-I hosted
the Essence Music Festival

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:04.203
a couple of years ago,

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.537
and Solange
was one of the performers.

00:05:05.537 --> 00:05:07.607
And as a host,
you get to see the sound check.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:12.945
And I wish everyone
had the opportunity to watch

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:16.349
the gift that is an
artist preparing and rehearsing.

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:18.951
And what she did was
so methodical and scientific

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.352
in how she presented her art.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:23.556
Like, it literally changed
the DNA of me as a performer.

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:24.924
So to be able to
have a conversation,

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.492
to ask a bunch of
questions about that,

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.327
like, that would be
the ultimate.

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:29.928
And Sam Jackson, I just want to
borrow one of his Kangols.

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:31.364
-Yeah, man, I get it.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.833
I think he always comes with
like a suitcase full of them,

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:34.934
so that's --

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.469
-He got 'em
in his hip like Batman.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.372
He "bap-bap" and put one on.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.006
-Hey, man,
thank you for being here.

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:42.642
It's always such a pleasure.
-I appreciate you, brother.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:43.809
-Happy New Year.
-Good to see you.

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:45.110
-Roy Wood Jr.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.280
The "The Daily Show" returns
from hiatus January 17th.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.749
We'll be right back.

